One parentless baseline: 20261008_0062. Frozen SQL includes durable relations,
checkpoints, views, functions, triggers, constraints, and pg_trgm; Python metadata
is incomplete. No corpus rows, local-state transfers, or historical installers.
Future migrations descend from it. Bootstrap, historical upgrades, and recovery:
../docs/operations.md#database-tools.

Catalog administration full-text indexes
---------------------------------------
20261011_0063 descends from the frozen baseline and adds GIN expression indexes
for titles, editions, raw/confirmed names, collections, and classification text.
The expressions use the explicit simple text-search configuration. They match
Yaruq Admin's per-column full-text predicates; existing trigram indexes remain
available for literal contains and PostgreSQL regex matching. This migration
adds no generated columns and changes no publication/document contents.

Use the separately configured Alembic workflow described in the database-tools
section of ../docs/operations.md. Review the new migration, then apply it before
rolling out the admin search feature:

    PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/alembic upgrade head

The admin application and Manzara task startup do not apply migrations.
Concurrent index builds allow catalog writers to continue, but require schema
ownership privileges and consume CPU/storage. Each build commits separately;
completion advances alembic_version_manzara only after every build succeeds.
There is no fixed duration guarantee. Monitor PostgreSQL's pg_stat_progress_create_index
while an authorized build is running.

If a build is interrupted or fails, leave the database version at its current
revision. Inspect pg_index.indisvalid and pg_get_indexdef for the six index names
listed in 20261011_0063_catalog_search_indexes.py. Review each existing definition
against that migration, then explicitly DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY for only these
new indexes before retrying the upgrade. Run each drop outside a transaction;
do not drop existing trigram indexes, modify catalog data, or stamp the revision.
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS is deliberately avoided because it can skip invalid
indexes and incorrectly make the migration appear complete.

Downgrading this revision drops only these six indexes concurrently and returns
to 20261008_0062; baseline rollback remains unavailable. SQL can be reviewed
without applying it using the selected private configuration:

    PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/alembic upgrade 20261008_0062:head --sql

Follow ../docs/verification.md: the default checks are inspection and static
verification. Database migration tests require an explicit owner request and
an isolated PostgreSQL with test-only configuration.
